  "notes": "Cash-basis county; governmental funds only, no business-type funds. Pages (trimmed): 1 Net Position, 2 Activities, 3-4 fund balances (p4 total column), 5-6 governmental funds receipts/disbursements (p6 total column), 7-8 General Fund combining, 9-10 nonmajor combining (Total Non-Major column on p10), 11-12 General Fund budget, 13 Road, 14 ARP, 15 Road and Bridge, 16 budget note. Taxes 4,649,547 split into property, motor vehicle and lodging using Statement of Activities general receipts (p2), which sum exactly. Local 1,279,465 (p6) split using the Statement of Activities (p2): interest income 303,411 and miscellaneous 84,040 (general receipts that can only sit in Local), remainder 892,014 charges for services/fees (computed, review). SOA charges for services 1,897,510 = Local remainder 892,014 + 1,005,496 of Intergovernmental shown as program receipts. Sale of surplus 23,965 is printed under Other Financing Sources so recorded in other_financing. Transfers in/out 1,750,000 each net to zero. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p11, budget basis; its Local actual 1,071,626 includes sale of surplus 6,510, and it excludes Inheritance Tax, Self-Health, Veterans Aid and Noxious Weed sub-funds, which come from the combining page p7-8); General Fund column of combining page not recorded to avoid double counting. Road fund budget-basis Local 39,438 includes sale of surplus 17,455. Nonmajor funds (10 columns) recorded using the Total column. Road fund spending has no function detail so recorded as streets/highways not itemized. Transfer cross-check: GF transfers out 1,412,186 = Self-Health in 112,219 + Noxious Weed in 49,967 + Road in 1,100,000 + other (Road and Bridge 500,000 from Road; Courthouse 150,000 nonmajor); totals tie at 1,750,000 in/out statement-wide. Read pages 1-16 of 16"
}
